('options', 'Options', 'Trade listed US equity options with defined risk: buy calls or puts (and spreads only if the account level allows) where the expected move around a dated catalyst, an earnings print, or a measured technical range is larger than what the implied volatility prices in. Work the chain: read /data/option-chain/<underlying> for quotes, greeks and implied volatility, compare realised versus implied volatility, pick expiries that outlast the catalyst by at least a week, and keep strikes near the money so the position survives a partial move. Size by premium: contracts cost qty x price x 100, so one contract is often the whole allowed position; never let a single premium exceed the fund cap. Stops and targets are on the option price, not the underlying. Backtest the setup on the underlying first, record every analysis, and quote the source for each catalyst.', 0.15, 'active', '2026-09-02T00:00:00.000Z');
